// North-row lot (housing frame, top-middle slot) — same dir="up"
// orientation as the Mansion: native y=0 is the far-from-road content,
// native y=HEIGHT is nearest the road.
//
// Source photo showed a two-house repeat with no clean per-lot seam (the
// garage/driveway sit off-center within each repeat, bleeding across any
// simple half-width split). Extraction re-cropped wider (source x 0-656,
// not 0-620) to land on the clean gap between this lot's own border tree
// row and the next repeat's, instead of cutting through a tree — see the
// half-tree-fix commit. That width change shifts the vertical scale on
// everything below it (still scaled to fit the lot by width only).
//
// Also fixes an overcorrection from squishing the fence/hedge/flower-bed
// band down to match the Mansion's: the total photo ended up shorter
// than the space above the road, so drawGroundImageLot's dir="up"
// leftover-fill kicked in and painted flat lawn-green across the WHOLE
// gap between the photo and the top of the screen, instead of the photo
// just reaching it — a much bigger, more obvious gap than intended.
// Fixed by extending the garage segment up to the very top of the
// source photo (0, not 90) to add back real tree-row content instead of
// leaving it for the fallback to fill, and sized the padding past the
// gate to land the total right at that same budget on purpose (~642px
// at this lot's scale) so the photo's own top edge reaches the screen's
// top edge with nothing but a sliver of intentional overshoot, same as
// the Mansion.
//
// Keeps most of the garage, the full house, and the complete fence/
// hedge/flower-bed band scaled down to match the Mansion's much sparser
// fence, padded with flat lawn-green past the gate so the north
// sidewalk's hidden zone eats only that padding.
